  "body": "## What happens\n\nA comparison of `main` (`4d891498e`) against the tool library mockup (#3663) found these small layout faults after the refit U8 to U12:\n\n1. Tool editor: the side drawing is small, and its dimension labels overlap and are clipped. Fit the drawing to the pane.\n2. Tool list: at the docked width, the Recipes column is clipped and the \"in document\" badge does not show.\n3. Holders list: the \"Used by\" column is cut off at the right edge. Shrink the other columns.\n4. Tool editor, Assembly section: the explanation, the total gauge length, the clamping check and the \"Open holder\" link are below the fold. Show them without a scroll.\n5. Recipes tab: put the derived line (Vc, fz) under each row, not under the table. Hide the \"Unknown\" row when the stock material has its own row. Stop the wrap of the \"Copy recipes from tool\" button.\n6. Tool list: the row thumbnail is a thin sliver. Draw a small tool with its holder, and show the holder text as \"BT40 ER32 x 70\".\n\n## Evidence\n\nThe comparison files are local notes of the reporter (renders `r2-*.png` and `GAPS-r2.md`). The PR adds before and after screenshots of each item.\n\n## Done means\n\n- Each item above is fixed, or the PR says why it is left as it is.\n- The layout tests of the touched pages (`layout_window_*`, `layout_page_*`) are updated. The `crates/ui` test count does not go down (#1953).\n- Before and after screenshots for each item.\n\nNote: #4453 changes the Recipes tab (feed per tooth and mm/min). Item 5 builds on it.\n",
